Pyro patch 0044: an import map scope keyed by a referring script's exact URL is in the resolved module set.

HTML "merge existing and new import maps" step 3.1 drops a new scope rule when a pair of the resolved
module set has a referring script that starts with the scope prefix and a specifier that equals or
starts with the rule's specifier. JSC keeps that set as, per referring-script prefix, the specifiers
resolved, but findURLPrefixes only yields the prefixes that end in '/': a scope keyed by the referring
script's whole URL (no trailing '/') never found its resolutions, so a second import map could change
what an already resolved specifier meant for that script. The whole URL is a prefix of itself too.
WPT import-maps/multiple-import-maps/exact-url-scope-immutability.html.

diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/ImportMap.cpp b/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/ImportMap.cpp
index d20493a..ad77559 100644
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/ImportMap.cpp
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/ImportMap.cpp
@@ -454,6 +454,9 @@ void ImportMap::addModuleToResolvedModuleSet(String referringScriptURL, AtomStri
         m_toplevelResolvedModuleSet.add(specifierPrefix);
 
     Vector<AtomString> referringScriptPrefixes = findURLPrefixes(referringScriptURL);
+    // A scope key that is the referring script's whole URL (no trailing '/') is a prefix of it too:
+    // "does not start with scopePrefix" (merge step 3.1.1) lets an equal string through.
+    referringScriptPrefixes.append(AtomString(referringScriptURL));
     for (AtomString& referringScriptPrefix : referringScriptPrefixes) {
         const auto& currentSetIt = m_scopedResolvedModuleMap.find(referringScriptPrefix);
         UncheckedKeyHashSet<AtomString>* currentSet = nullptr;
